 {
-  "description": "Create, update or delete skills: your procedural memory for recurring tasks. The call is an operations array (a single edit is a list of one); it applies atomically — any failure rolls every touched skill back. Ops: create (full SKILL.md; lands in the profile's skills directory or configured skills.create_dir; must precede that skill's other ops), patch (targeted old_string/new_string fix — preferred; content alone REPLACES the whole file, read it via skill_view() first), write_file/remove_file (supporting files), delete (sole op only). Existing skills are modified wherever they live. Description: max 60 chars, 'Use when <trigger>. <behavior>.', never the category name (the index shows it). Write lessons, not logs: imperative rule + why, no PR numbers/dates/incident narration, one rule per lesson, references/ named by topic (extend before adding). skill_view() shows format conventions.",
+  "description": "Create, update or delete skills: your procedural memory for recurring tasks. The call is an operations array (a single edit is a list of one); it applies atomically — any failure rolls every touched skill back. Ops: create (full SKILL.md; lands in the profile's skills directory or configured skills.create_dir; must precede that skill's other ops), patch (targeted old_string/new_string fix — preferred; content alone REPLACES the whole file, read it via skill_view() first), write_file/remove_file (supporting files), delete (sole op only). Existing skills are modified wherever they live. Description: max 60 chars, 'Use when <trigger>. <behavior>.' with the trigger in the user's own words, never the category name (the index shows it); a skill easily confused with another adds frontmatter triggers: {asks: [3 user phrasings], not_for: '<task> (use <skill>)'}. Write lessons, not logs: imperative rule + why, no PR numbers/dates/incident narration, one rule per lesson, references/ named by topic (extend before adding). skill_view() shows format conventions.",
